    description: "FOUND by WI-tusad F2 (finding 4, ledger), re-stated by F3. The OCaml analyzer registers type and module symbols in symbol_by_name, so a call can bind to a TYPE. After F2 named nested types with their module (`A.t`), 16 of 17 such calls on a 723-node OCaml sample now reach the function; 1 still binds a type: `mime_type` -> type `Destination.path` (b8a corpus, ocaml). Fix: keep non-callable kinds out of the call-resolution table (or filter by kind at resolution). Not measured beyond the 40-file sample."  # dd80
    fields: {}  # dd80
